{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "description": "Waiting for a hub to admit a new connection: about ninety seconds while the platform carries the client to its hub. The wait follows the operation the create answered with, polling GET /v1/operations/{id} (its links.self) every poll_interval_seconds. 'ready' is 'admitted'; 'failed' and 'timed_out' are 'failed', with the operation's error_code; requested, committed and applied keep polling. No operation at all, and a 404 (the API no longer tracks it), are 'admitted' at once. A 5xx is ridden out. When timeout_seconds pass first the outcome is 'timeout', which is a connection error and a timeout at once: the connection may still be admitted later. A links.self on another origin than the API's is 'error' and is never fetched: the token goes nowhere else. polls counts the GETs sent.",
 "source": "thalovant-api app/routes/clients.py _accept_client_sync_operation, app/routes/operations.py, app/services/operation_convergence.py (#358)",
